  "body": "## Summary\n\nDepends on #347. Draft only; no merge, provider activation or production deployment.\n\n- Route active Datafast create/status and PayPal OAuth/create/capture/query/refund/webhook verification through the same HTTP boundary as PlaceToPay/PayPhone.\n- Enforce provider-scoped HTTPS destinations, no redirects, a separate TLS pool with implicit connection retries disabled, a 15-second total deadline, and a streaming one-MiB decompressed response limit.\n- Reject unsafe OAuth tokens and redact URL, JSON, HTTP and decompression errors. Preserve active request encodings, integer amounts, external bindings and PayPal idempotency headers.\n- Remove three unused legacy PayPal remote helpers, including an unused floating-point amount formatter. Public HTTP routes and DTOs are unchanged.\n- Document architecture, original audit gaps, compatibility, rollout/rollback and verification evidence in ADR 0117 and the payment runbooks.\n\n## Verified local evidence\n\nFinal code/test commit: `1c27d2d8561f1effa10e2bea7d12193249f36961` (production code `74ccf95942202a82c3ac67418ac91a0eea058951`). macOS, Stack/GHC 9.10.3, http-client 0.7.19, Node 24.8.0, disposable PostgreSQL 16.\n\n- Provider-focused Stack tests: **112 examples, 0 failures**, including 19 new synthetic transport cases; completion observed 2026-09-15T01:56:21Z.\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2,583 examples, 0 failures**, 27.1996 seconds; completion observed 01:57:40Z.\n- `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh`: **36 PostgreSQL examples, 0 failures**, 5.9495 seconds; completion observed 01:58:27Z. Harness refuses non-test/populated databases and removed its own container.\n- Catalog audit with the existing `--fail-on-unreviewed` gate: **1,413 files / 1,122 candidates; zero unreviewed/stale decisions** on both runs. No audit gate or decision edits.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nThe in-memory HTTP fixtures exercise the real executor without network sockets or real TLS/provider access. They cover host tampering, redirects, overflow, stalled bodies, malformed JSON/HTTP/gzip, cookie policy, stale-connection POST retry suppression, token safety and stable create/capture references. Unit/fixture compilation failures and exact commands are preserved in `docs/payments/http-boundary-2026-09-14.md`; they are not omitted from the record. The test harness's deprecated public `closeManager` cleanup warning is not suppressed.\n\n## Compatibility / configuration / risks\n\n- No migration, backfill, new secret, historical record mutation or API/client schema change.\n- Existing feature flags, account evidence and environment gates remain. Datafast retains its validated oppwa.com origin family; merchant-specific endpoints remain unverified.\n- Legacy transport failures consistently return redacted HTTP 502 (some PayPal paths previously used 503). Neither code means no charge: retain the original attempt and reconcile before any retry/fallback.\n- A slow provider may produce more pending reconciliation outcomes under the hard deadline. Qualify real sandbox latency and response sizes before rollout; do not bypass limits or enable retries from an ambiguous result.\n- Historical payload retention, full adapter-domain consolidation, recurring flows and marketplace payout authority remain outside this patch.\n- No frontend/native-device, real TLS/provider sandbox or staging payment tests were executed for this backend-only change. Staging authentication and merchant credentials/contracts remain unavailable/unverified; see #344.\n\n## Review / rollback\n\nOrder: #331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 #347 \u2192 this PR. #344 is independent after #343.\n\nRollback is code-only and restores weaker transport protections; prefer a reviewed forward fix. Stop new payment writes through an approved operational procedure, preserve attempts/events/external IDs and reconcile original references. Do not clear financial records or issue replacement charges.\n\nNo screenshots were produced for this internal backend change. Remote CI results must be evaluated on this PR's exact head; parent #347's green checks are not substituted for this patch.\n",
